PS2Recomp HLE kernel adaptation
Upstream: https://github.com/ran-j/PS2Recomp
Revision: e5636981a1c9de368f6b71e819c3dc188dfedbf4
License: GPL-3.0 (see LICENSE in this directory)
Credit: PS2Recomp contributors. Existing ps2-native code retains its BSD notices.

Adapted source files:
ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/EeScheduler.cpp
ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/Syscalls/Dispatcher.cpp
ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/Syscalls/Thread.cpp
ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/Syscalls/Sync.cpp
ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/Syscalls/System.cpp
ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/Syscalls/Helpers/State.h

The adaptation reuses kernel object allocation, EE descriptors/error codes,
semaphore/event algorithms and thread lifecycle. Context/memory access,
dispatch and scheduling use ps2-native EEState, Memory and clocks.
No standalone upstream runtime, second memory/device state, host-clock VBLANK scheduler,
game overrides or success stubs are linked. Device IRQ wakeups, alarms, file/RPC
services and HLE checkpoint serialization are not implemented in this subset.

Combined binaries linking this GPL component must be distributed under the
GPL-3.0 terms, with corresponding source and the applicable license notices.

SDK integration: ps2xAnalyzer and ps2xRecomp are built from the same pinned
PS2Recomp revision through cmake/PS2Recomp.cmake. Sources remain in the SDK
checkout (PS2N_PS2RECOMP_SOURCE_DIR); deps.lock.json records the revision,
transitive dependency revisions and reproducible patches in patches/ps2recomp.
Local changes: embeddable CMake paths, host-controlled compiler policy and
UTF-8 file paths, checked output writes and explicit error queries in the
recompiler. Upstream authorship/notices are preserved.
The SDK PS2Runtime class now has an exclusive integrated native backend,
implemented in src/ps2recomp_runtime.cpp, owning the platform CPU, Memory,
NVM and adapted HLE kernel. The standalone SDK memory, GS, scheduler and
VU/IOP interpreters are excluded from that backend. The generated R5900Context
ABI and remaining upstream services are not yet connected to this owner.
SDK tools and combined binaries require
GPL-3.0 distribution terms and corresponding source, including these patches;
the original platform code retains its BSD-3-Clause notices. Dependencies
retain their own licenses and notices in their pinned source trees.
